uid "1331e652-c61f-5c8e-a6f4-74a3f821bc65" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186552925 #edb/ref 1080 "$U=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} & \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{aligned}]$\nand\n$V=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}]$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186552925 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186552925 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "1f0d9999-e6b0-5c01-ba6c-7b00ae306da2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186552986 #edb/ref 1080 "$U=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]$ and $V=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}]$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186552986 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186552986 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "3aab75be-ac8f-51df-a5c8-7c427cf91fca" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553018 #edb/ref 1080 "$U=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} & \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}]$\nand\n$V=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}]$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553018 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553018 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "47f5a809-544a-582b-a596-10978b78f520" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553235 #edb/ref 1080 "$U=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{3}{5} & \\frac{4}{5} \\\\ \\frac{4}{5} & \\frac{3}{5}\\end{aligned}]$\nand\n$V=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{5} & -\\frac{4}{5} \\\\ \\frac{4}{5} & \\frac{3}{5}\\end{aligned}]$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553235 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553235 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "b897c736-6978-5c1a-82c7-2ca2fd4d1abc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553398 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186552901 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553398 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186552925 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553398 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186552986 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553398 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186553018 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553398 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186553235 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553398 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553398 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553398 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186552986 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553398 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "3919e73a-7fa3-5959-8a80-51de4cf465ae" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553538 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186553398 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553538 #edb/ref 1069 "q-96300" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553538 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553538 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,Σ=[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrices $A$ and $Σ$ shown above. Given that $A=UΣ{V}^{T}$ is a singular value decomposition of $A,$ which of the following could be the matrices $U$ and $V?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553538 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "7a667003-8ac5-5712-9785-d67340dc0f82" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553538 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's find the singular value decomposition of $A$ using the usual algorithm.\n\n- **Step 1.** Compute ${A}^{T}\\,A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,A & ={[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]}^{T}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- **Step 2.** Find the singular values: Notice that from the matrix $Σ,$ we can deduce that ${\\sigma }_{1}=\\sqrt{2}$ and ${\\sigma }_{2}=0$ without solving the characteristic equation.\n\n- **Step 3.** Find the right singular vectors of $A$ (i.e., the unit eigenvectors of ${A}^{T}\\,A$):\n\n- For ${\\lambda }_{1}={\\sigma }_{1}^{2}=2,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,A-2I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]-2[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSeeking a non-zero solution of $({A}^{T}\\,A-2I)v=0$ gives a unit eigenvector\n\n$$\n{v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n- For ${\\lambda }_{2}={\\sigma }_{2}^{2}=0,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,A-0I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]-0[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSeeking a non-zero solution of $({A}^{T}\\,A-0I)v=0$ gives a unit eigenvector\n\n$$\n{v}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n- **Step 4.** Find the left singular vectors of $A$ (i.e., the unit eigenvectors of $A{A}^{T}$): Since the first singular value is not zero, and we know the corresponding singular right vector, we can compute the first column of $U$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}_{1} & =\\frac{1}{{\\sigma }_{1}}A{v}_{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the second singular value is ${\\sigma }_{2}=0$, we can't use the same formula to find the second column of $U.$ But we know that $U$ must be orthogonal. Hence, we must find a vector\n\n$$\n{u}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nsuch that \n\n$$\n{u}_{1}\\cdot {u}_{2}=0\\,\\text{and}\\,‖{u}_{2}‖=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nSolving ${u}_{1}\\cdot {u}_{2}=0,$ which is equivalent to\n\n$$\n-{x}_{1}+0{x}_{2}=0,\n$$\n\nwe get the solution \n\n$$\n{u}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFinally, we construct the matrices $U$ and $V:$\n\n$$\nU=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,V=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}]\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553615 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186553682 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553615 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "3a2cb110-a121-50e5-98e3-664e4716991a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553615 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186553538 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553622 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186553623 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553622 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "585b7b68-1beb-5e64-886d-4e1b2b983b3e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553622 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186167426 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553623 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186553615 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553623 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "58dd1f4d-824a-5f34-bd20-21ac3f40bf35" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553623 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186371346 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553643 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "87a52191-3101-58ef-a6bb-fa008fb74e7a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553643 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186167468 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553682 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186553643 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553682 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "f52cf900-2792-505e-b166-a75202379c51" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553682 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186371388 #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
